<title>FRANCE: ROWING-WORLD CUP REGATTA RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ROWING-WORLD CUP REGATTA RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the first day of a</p>
<p>three-day World Cup rowing regatta on Friday:</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>Single sculls (winner to semifinals, rest to repechage)</p>
<p>Heat 1</p>
<p> 1. Iztok Cop (Slovenia)	    7 minutes 03.62 seconds</p>
<p>Heat 2</p>
<p> 1. Fredrik Bekken (Norway)			     7:07.26</p>
<p>Heat 3</p>
<p> 1. Ibrahim Ali (Egypt)				   7:02.29</p>
<p>Coxless pairs (winner to final, rest to repechage)</p>
<p>Heat 1</p>
<p>1. France 1 (Vincent Malizewski, Bernard Roche)  6:29.97</p>
<p>Heat 2</p>
<p> 1. Lituania (Einius Petkus, Juozas Bagdonas)     6:41.83</p>
<p>Lightweight double sculls (first 3 to semifinals, rest to</p>
<p>repechage)</p>
<p>Heat 1</p>
<p> 1. Switzerland (Markus Gier, Michael Gier)	 6:28.81</p>
<p> 2. France 1 (Frederic Dufour, Pascal Touron)     6:30.35</p>
<p> 3. Poland (Tomasz Fizka, Robert Sycz)		6:37.34</p>
<p>Heat 2</p>
<p> 1. Germany (Ingo Euler, Bernhard Rahling)	  6:29.58</p>
<p>2. Austria (Martin Kobau, Helfried Jurfschitsch) 5:35.28</p>
<p> 3. Britain 1 (Ned Kittoe, Stuart Forbes)	   6:37.29</p>
<p>Women</p>
